or case: State v. Nave\">694 S. W. 2d 729</a></span>; No. 85-6168, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1871100\"><a href=\"/opinion/1871100/billiot-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Billiot v. State\">478 So. 2d 1043</a></span>; No. 85-6228, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1688912\"><a href=\"/opinion/1688912/hooper-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Hooper v. State\">476 So. 2d 1253</a></span>; No. 85-6342, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1103847\"><a href=\"/opinion/1103847/wilcher-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Wilcher v. State\">479 So. 2d 710</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9053533,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":597,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b1073-5\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"AU0Z\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b1073-6\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}